# ---- Part two: reachability
C(ALL, "Callee gas: can an ordinary account make a precompile, predeploy or system contract that burns forwarded gas the recipient of a take or native payout, the hook or a currency inside a transaction that a victim sends through a normal router on an honest pool (lead L-684).",
  "No on all 21 networks, on the text of the code. The PoolManager makes outbound calls at four places only: the native payout and the token transfer of src/types/Currency.sol:48 and :73, whose target is the currency of the take and whose recipient is the `to` argument chosen by the caller of take (src/PoolManager.sol:291-297); the balanceOf staticcall of sync at src/types/Currency.sol:94, whose currency the caller chooses (src/PoolManager.sol:279-288); the hook call of src/libraries/Hooks.sol:134, whose target is key.hooks, part of the PoolKey that the pool id hashes (src/PoolManager.sol:132, 151); and the unlock callback to msg.sender (src/PoolManager.sol:110). In a victim's swap or removal on an honest pool, the currencies and the hook are fixed by the pool and the recipient and the callback target are fixed by the victim's router and calldata. No storage that a third party can write steers any of these targets. A gas-burning address can therefore appear only in a transaction the attacker builds, where it costs the attacker gas and reverts the attacker's own unlock. Where a hook address is a special address, the low 14 bits decide which callbacks run: HyperEVM 0x0800 to 0x0813 all set BEFORE_ADD_LIQUIDITY (Hooks.sol:32), so no deposit can enter such a pool; Monad 0x1000 sets AFTER_INITIALIZE (Hooks.sol:30), so the pool cannot be created; Arc 0x1800..00 has no flag bits and is never called. Gas forwarding is 63/64 everywhere except MegaETH (98/100), so after a callee burns its gas the PoolManager keeps at least 1/64 to revert. A victim's swap or removal therefore cannot be made to fail or to cost far more on any of the 21 networks through callee gas.",
  "src/types/Currency.sol:48, src/types/Currency.sol:73, src/types/Currency.sol:94, src/PoolManager.sol:110, src/PoolManager.sol:132, src/PoolManager.sol:151, src/PoolManager.sol:279-297, src/libraries/Hooks.sol:30-47, src/libraries/Hooks.sol:109-124, src/libraries/Hooks.sol:134; " + CG)
C(ALL, "Whether any client override found in this unit changes what the PoolManager computes, as opposed to gas.",
  "No. The handlers replaced on Arc (SELFDESTRUCT, value-call frame hook, CallFrom intercept), MegaETH (gas wrappers, 98/100 forwarding, volatile guards), Tempo (0x4f, SSTORE, 0xef) and Nitro (GASPRICE, BLOCKHASH, NUMBER, SELFDESTRUCT, filter touches) leave every arithmetic, hashing, memory, return data and transient storage result unchanged. The PoolManager's five GAS reads only feed call gas, so a different amount of gas left cannot steer its logic. The one value-visible change is Arc's success flag for value calls to three recipient classes, recorded as the finding.",
  "research/network-risk/OPCODES.md lines 146, 118; " + ARC + "/evm/src/evm.rs; " + MEGA + "; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OffchainLabs/go-ethereum/0e44603/core/vm/instructions.go")

